# arm-index: baseline for the Appendix A <-> arm reconciliation.
#
# Format:  <key>  <reason>.  Key is `INV-x no-arm` or `INV-x back-pointer <CODE>`.
#
# BASELINE 2026-08-24, UNRESOLVED. These entries record the state at the moment
# the reconciliation pass was introduced -- not a verdict that they are correct.
# The point of this file is that the NEXT divergence does not pass unnoticed, the
# same arrangement .truth/label-coupling-opt-out uses for module pairs.
#
# The back-pointer class is populous for a structural reason, not from neglect:
# an arm declares a subject from ONE register (usually an ADR or an issue) while
# an Appendix A row points at it from another. Both names are correct, and the
# link is still one-way -- which is precisely why inverting an arm never reaches
# the row. Resolving each entry is separate work: either the arm names INV-x in
# its header, or the row stops naming it.
#
# The no-arm class is rows whose Gate names no arm this sweep can recognise.

